    Servo : signal=18   (power from a separate 5-6V supply, common ground)
    Magnet: control=23  (through a relay or MOSFET module, never directly from the pin)
    Metal : digital out=34, analog out=35 (3.3V max! use a divider/level shifter for 5V/12V sensors)
  ---------------------------------------------------------------------

  HTTP API (GET or POST, JSON replies):
    /api/status
    /api/move?dir=forward|backward|left|right|stop&speed=70
    /api/drive?left=-50&right=80
    /api/arm?pos=lower|raise|bin|stow      or   /api/arm?angle=0..180
    /api/magnet?state=on|off|toggle
    /api/sweep?state=start|stop
    /api/stop      (EMERGENCY STOP, latched)
    /api/resume    (clear emergency stop)

  BLE (Nordic UART style, text commands, one per write):
    move forward 70 | drive -50 80 | arm lower | arm angle 90 |
    magnet on | sweep start | stop | resume | status
    Replies: "OK", "ERR <reason>", or the status JSON for "status".

  SAFETY
    - Failsafe: robot stops if no drive command arrives within COMMAND_TIMEOUT_MS.
      The website must re-send the move command every ~150 ms while a button is held.
    - Emergency stop latches until resume.
    - Magnet auto-switches off after MAGNET_MAX_ON_MS (coil overheating protection).

